@startuml 10-activity-move
!include _style.iuml
title Applying a tree move safely (after Kleppmann et al.)

start
:receive move(t, node, new_parent);
if (t older than the latest applied op?) then (yes)
  :undo applied ops newer than t;
else (no)
endif
if (node == new_parent\nor node is an ancestor of new_parent?) then (would create a cycle)
  :record the move as a no-op;
else (safe)
  :set node.parent = new_parent;
endif
:redo the undone ops in timestamp order,\nre-checking each move the same way;
stop

note right
  Every replica applies moves in the same
  timestamp order, so every replica skips
  the same moves. The move skipped is the
  one that would close the cycle given the
  earlier ones, not "the older intent".
end note
@enduml
